# Graph Game — Project Rules

## Tech Stack
- React 18 + TypeScript 5 (strict mode)
- Vite
- SVG rendering for graph (no Canvas for MVP)
- Vitest + Testing Library for tests
- No backend, no database

## Coding Conventions
- NO `any` types — все типы явно объявлены
- Functional components + hooks only (no class components)
- File naming: kebab-case for files (`graph-generator.ts`), PascalCase for components (`GraphCanvas.tsx`)
- Every algorithm function must have JSDoc with complexity note
- No `console.log` in committed code

## Architecture
- `src/lib/graph/` — types, generator, algorithms (dijkstra, bfs)
- `src/components/` — React components
- `src/hooks/` — custom hooks
- Tests colocated with source: `graph-generator.test.ts` next to `graph-generator.ts`

## Graph Domain Rules
- Node type: `{ id: string; x: number; y: number }`
- Edge type: `{ from: string; to: string; weight: number }`
- Graph must ALWAYS be connected (validate after generation)
- Dijkstra returns `{ path: string[]; totalWeight: number }`

## Testing
- Test generator: "always produces connected graph for 100 random seeds"
- Test dijkstra: "returns correct path on known small graph"
- Run tests before any commit

## Git
- Conventional commits format
- Small atomic commits